{:id :EACL-FORMAL-096
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust/EACL-RS-002/expression-continuation-line"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0.0 commit a698b3bdf15e61be9bfd1324d7d7c67dc82176be"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "The Instaparse grammar ended every statement at a line break, so a permission expression or relation type list wrapped after a binary operator or '|' was a parse error, although SpiceDB v1.56.0 accepts it."
 :fix
 "Apply SpiceDB's synthetic-semicolon rule: a line end ends a statement only after a name, keyword, ')', '}' or '*'. After '+', '&', '-', '|', '->', ':' or '=' the statement continues on the next line, and a line that starts with an operator is still a parse error, as in SpiceDB."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/continuation-lines-test"
  "eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/spicedb-verdicts-test"]
 :notes
 "Found by the eacl-rust port (BUGS.md EACL-RS-002), verified against main a698b3bd and SpiceDB v1.56.0."}
